menu "LED strip (NeoPixel)"

    config LEDS_GPIO
        int "Data GPIO"
        default 16
        range 0 48
        help
            The strip's data line. 16 is P2 pin 8 on the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.28,
            the pin the Flash_PNG sketch drove its NeoPixels from (PIN_NEO_PIXEL).

    config LEDS_COUNT
        int "LEDs on the strip"
        default 16
        range 1 1024
        help
            Flash_PNG's NUM_PIXELS.

    choice LEDS_SPEED
        prompt "Data rate"
        default LEDS_SPEED_400K
        help
            Flash_PNG drove its strip at 400 kHz (NEO_KHZ400). That is the native rate of
            WS2811 driver chips and first-generation NeoPixels; WS2812/WS2812B/SK6812
            NeoPixels are 800 kHz parts, though most accept the 400 kHz timing too.

        config LEDS_SPEED_400K
            bool "400 kHz (WS2811; Flash_PNG's NEO_KHZ400)"
        config LEDS_SPEED_800K
            bool "800 kHz (WS2812, WS2812B, SK6812)"
    endchoice

    choice LEDS_ORDER
        prompt "Colour order on the wire"
        default LEDS_ORDER_GRB
        help
            Flash_PNG's NEO_GRB, and that of nearly every WS2812-family part. If red and
            green come out swapped, the strip is RGB.

        config LEDS_ORDER_GRB
            bool "GRB"
        config LEDS_ORDER_RGB
            bool "RGB"
    endchoice

    config LEDS_BRIGHTNESS
        int "Brightness at boot (percent)"
        default 100
        range 1 100
        help
            `leds bright` changes it live. Each LED draws up to about 60 mA at full white,
            so a 16-LED strip at 100% can want 1 A: more than the P2 header's VSYS pin and
            its SH1.0 contact should be asked for. Powering the strip from the header, keep
            this at 30 or below; powered from its own 5 V supply, leave it at 100.

endmenu
